ther it's true or not  and it's the win for hasselblad a pretty  traditional old-timey camera company who  can now associate their name with an  upstart trendy smartphone company to  signal that they're high-tech and  fashion-forward you know this happens  with leica all the time too so whether  they're cringy or super corporate or not  whatever the vibe is there are a number  of brand collabs all around the tech  industry every year that makes sense  and then there are  monstrosities like this because on the  surface in the tech world this seems  dumb it's a gucci xbox why would that be  better than a regular xbox does a gucci  xbox perform or play games better in  some way do i get anything out of having  a gucci xbox of course not but if you've  noticed there's actually been a lot of  tech collaborations like this tech  companies collaborating with fashion  companies fashion brands so tech  products are in this weird place where  most of the stuff you buy is supposed to  be purely functional right you buy a  piece of tech because it accomplishes a  task or serves a certain function it's a  computer that does the thing you need it  to but not necessarily because of the  fashion  but whether we like to admit it or not  there is a personal element to all these  purchases i've always said the  smartphone you buy is actually one of  the most personal choices you make you  hold it every day you take it everywhere  with you it wakes you up in the morning  you feel kind of empty and lost without  it so even though it is just a piece of  tech it's no wonder the companies that  sell them want you to feel like they're  also pretty fashionable in addition to  being a good piece of tech you might  remember lg collaborated with prada on  smartphones three different times  samsung collaborated with hugo boss on a  smartphone back in 2008 and again in  2011 louis vuitton collaborated recently  with headphone maker master and dynamic  to sell some 995 earbuds there was a  gold dolce gabbana razor three a decade  ago and i think apple and hermes may be  the best example of them all  hermes  i never know if i'm saying that right  hermes  hermes hermes right but i just remember  so distinctly when the apple watch went  on sale the first one went on sale back  in 2015  and apple they of course made a couple  versions there was a black version and a  silver version it was stainless steel  but they wanted to of course signify  that it was fashionable because it's a  watch and they have to get the fashion  crowd to like it and so they made the  apple watch edition and this version was  plated in solid 18 karat gold and it  started at ten thousand dollars now  anybody already subscribed here to this  channel probably already knows that it's  a bad idea to drop 10 bands on a first  gen tech product  just because it's covered in gold and  you think it's fashionable but that  that's that's a real thing people did  that's out there like the real humans  actually spent that money on the first  gen apple watch tech blogs had a field  day with the headlines we already knew  this was coming but yeah a year later  there was a new one the addition was  discontinued  of course it turns out apple even as  massive and popular and successful and  wealthy as they are can't break into  fashion immediately just by themselves  on their own name and so shortly after  that we did see the beginning of that  hermes collaboration so that fashion  brand comes in they start to do custom  watch bands unique styles with leather  that match the watch faces and custom  packaging and higher prices because you  know it's fashion that's kind of the way  things work but that that collaboration  has been way more successful it  continues to this day and it's a win-win  for both companies hermes gets a much  more tech focused crowd and apple gets  to break into the much more  fashion-centric crowd so fundamentally  that's what they're always looking for  in these brand collaborations is a win  for both sides that win-win  kind of like mkbhd  and new channel sponsor cash app cash  app is incredible i get to share with  you guys they're the easiest way to send  spend and save money and you can buy  stocks or even bitcoin with a dollar so  if you use code marquez to sign up 15  bucks will appear in your account it's  not bad and then 10 will go to girls who  code link below but the point is the  point is this none of these  tech fashion collabs actually makes the  product better like  none of them that's not the point of  this type of collab now you could argue  that the tech on tech collabs actually  do you could say if oneplus and  hasselblad are collaborating that that  actually can make the camera in the  phone a bit better you could argue that  you could argue the nike plus and apple  sponsorship and collaboration actually  made a better product but  this is just a monogrammed  xbox series x it's not a better xbox uh  the dolce gabbana razer was just a gold  razor it's more about the experience of  taking it out of the box the custom  packaging the fashion nature of it  whatever you think about this fashion  that's what that collab is more about  and then there's also the x factor which  is just hype so brands have various  levels of this and in a world where the  playstation 5 from rival sony was pretty  much the most hyped thing in gaming for  a whole year around its release i mean  it's still impossible to get so  microsoft and their brand team is of  course looking for ways to get people  talking about and thinking about xbox  series x which came out around the same  time and what better way than by  creating a limited edition super hyped  special xbox with one of the most hyped  companies so even though the product  isn't actually better the hype and all  the brand awareness created by this  collab  is a win-win for both companies so  that's why the gucci xbox exists this  honestly probably would have been  received the exact same way if it was a  supreme xbox or i don't know louis  vuitton xbox it's just they just want  people saying xbox more you know and  it's working  is it's working isn't it i'm here  sitting on video talking about it and  now it's on youtube going into their  brand sentiment calculator and of course  there's no dislikes on this video so it  must be working but yeah the truth is i  divided them into two different  categories at the beginning of this  video those that seem to make sense and  those that don't but at the end of the  day when you look at it as a win-win in  some way they kind of all do make some  level of sense so i wouldn't be shocked  if we keep seeing  more of this type of stuff  thanks for watching catch the next one  peace  [Music]

